# `vite build --mode preview` produces the build we hand to a static host that
# has no SPA rewrite rule. Hash routing is what makes a deep link survive a
# refresh there. src/main.jsx reads this; vite.config.js sets the matching
# relative base.
#
# Vite only exposes variables it loads from a .env file, so this cannot be a
# shell variable — as a shell variable it silently does nothing and the preview
# build quietly ships BrowserRouter.
VITE_HASH_ROUTER=true
